  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0031-p00031",
      "source_en": "Hurry, hurry, hurry! Drive it on, drive it on, drive it on! A roll of smoke, a strip of mountain, a few cloud-shadows, A sweep of water, a bridge, a stroke of oar-sound, A forest of pines, a clump of bamboos, red leaves in a scatter: Fields flushed with color, an autumn scene in deep hues, As clear as a dream, then hazy, then fading away—, Drive it on, drive it on, drive it on! Is it the wheel, or is it time? It has worn autumn itself old, and it has worn life itself old. Written on October 30, 1923.",
      "units": [
